WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Cauliflower Gratin. 50 min · 8 servings · American

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Ingredients: 12. 2 cauliflower heads; 1 cup+ Parmesan and sharp cheddar cheese (mix); 1/2 cup butter; 1 cup panko crumbs

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Step 1. Wash and cut cauliflower into bite-size pieces.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Step 2. Boil or steam florets till slight crisp, about 10–15 min.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Step 3. Melt 2–3 tablespoons butter over medium heat; add panko crumbs and stir till slightly toasted.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Step 4. Add 1 tablespoon garlic powder and 1 tablespoon onion powder to the panko crumbs.

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Step 5. Place half of the florets into a blender; pulse till smooth.

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Step 6. Add cheese, mustard, nutmeg, cayenne, salt, and pepper to the mixture and blend till smooth and creamy. May need to add milk to create a thick sauce.

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Step 7. In a 9x9 pan: place whole florets in the pan, pour blended sauce on top, and stir well.

10
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Step 8. Place panko crumbs on top.

11
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Step 9. Bake at 400°F for 30 min+.

12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.000
You're ready. Use Make It for checkboxes on the page.
